WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:05.634
♪♪

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:09.434
Narrator:
STAND-UP PADDLING HAS BECOME
A POPULAR SPORT,

00:00:09.434 --> 00:00:13.000
BUT PADDLE BOARDS HAVE BEEN
AROUND FOR OVER 3,000 YEARS.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.100
CONTEMPORARY BOARDS RELY ON
MODERN MATERIALS TO MAKE LIGHT

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.400
AND RELIABLE PADDLE BOARDS
SUITED FOR LEISURE,

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.367
AS WELL AS FOR COMPETITION.

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:25.801
♪♪

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:28.834
THIS PADDLE BOARD IS MADE WITH
VINYL ESTER RESIN

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:30.467
AND LAMINATED FIBERGLASS.

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:33.801
IT'S EQUIPPED WITH AN ON-BOARD
LIGHTING SYSTEM, AN ANCHOR,

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:36.968
AND A NEOPRENE RUBBER
NON-SLIP PAD.

00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:39.767
IN THE GEL-COATING ROOM,
A TECHNICIAN

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:43.067
WIPES A RELEASE AGENT
ON THE PADDLE BOARD MOLD,

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:45.868
TO MAKE THE SURFACE SMOOTH
AND CLEAN.

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:51.434
ANOTHER TECHNICIAN POSITIONS THE
FIN CHANNEL ON THE MOLD

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:55.968
USING A THIN FIBERGLASS TEMPLATE
AS A GUIDE.

00:00:55.968 --> 00:00:59.334
HE USES AN AIRLESS PUMPING
SYSTEM TO SPRAY THE MOLD

00:00:59.334 --> 00:01:02.767
WITH A VINYL ESTER GEL COATING
MIXED WITH HARDENER.

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:07.834
♪♪

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:14.033
HE TAKES A MILL GAUGE TO MAKE
SURE THE HULL THICKNESS IS EVEN.

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:17.501
A TECHNICIAN PREPARES TO MAKE
THE FIRST STRUCTURAL LAYER

00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:19.601
OF THE HULL,
USING A 3/4 OUNCE

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:21.467
BI-DIRECTIONAL FIBERGLASS MAT.

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:22.634
♪♪

00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:25.667
FIRST, HE PULLS OUT
A PANEL OF FIBERGLASS

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:28.300
AND COVERS
THE GEL-COATED SURFACE.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:32.534
USING FABRIC SCISSORS,
HE CUTS THE MAT

00:01:32.534 --> 00:01:37.968
AND MAKES THE FIBERGLASS SKIN
AS TIGHT AS POSSIBLE.

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:39.968
HE TEARS THE MAT
TO CONFORM IT

00:01:39.968 --> 00:01:42.300
TO THE ROUNDED SHAPE OF
THE GEL COAT.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:47.167
AND FITS THE MAT
TO THE EDGE OF THE HULL.

00:01:47.167 --> 00:01:50.968
HE APPLIES VINYL ESTER RESIN
WITH A PAINT ROLLER.

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:53.467
THE RESIN SATURATES THE
FIBERGLASS,

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:55.934
WHICH MERGES WITH
THE GEL COATING.

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:57.968
♪♪

00:01:57.968 --> 00:02:01.667
EXTRA MATERIAL IS PLACED OVER
THE FIN CHANNEL TO STRENGTHEN

00:02:01.667 --> 00:02:05.000
THE STRUCTURAL BOND BETWEEN THE
CHANNEL AND THE HULL.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.701
♪♪

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:12.667
THEN, THE TECHNICIAN
USES A BUBBLE ROLLER

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:14.968
TO PUSH OUT AIR BUBBLES.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:18.367
HE APPLIES A SECOND COAT
OF FIBERGLASS

00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:22.701
TO REINFORCE THE STRUCTURAL
INTEGRITY OF THE BOARD.

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:25.167
IN THE ASSEMBLY ROOM,
ANOTHER TECHNICIAN

00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:27.300
FITS A TEMPLATE
ON THE BOARD DECK

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:31.033
AND TRACES THE CONTOURS OF THE
HAND-GRAB MOUNT WITH A PENCIL.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:35.033
♪♪

00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:39.133
HE USES AN AIR SAW TO CUT OUT A
SLOT IN THE FIBERGLASS LAMINATE

00:02:39.133 --> 00:02:40.667
TO FIT THE HAND-GRAB MOUNT.

00:02:40.667 --> 00:02:46.167
♪♪

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:49.033
HE BINDS THE HAND-GRAB MOUNT TO
THE HOLE WITH A COAT

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:51.701
OF VINYL ESTER RESIN.

00:02:51.701 --> 00:02:56.834
WITHIN ABOUT 20 MINUTES,
THE LAMINATE HARDENS.

00:02:56.834 --> 00:03:00.100
NEXT, PLASTIC TUBING FOR
THE INTERNAL ANCHORING SYSTEM

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:01.434
IS INSTALLED.

00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:05.133
A TECHNICIAN APPLIES A BONDING
ADHESIVE TO THE TUBE,

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:06.734
SECURING IT IN PLACE.

00:03:06.734 --> 00:03:09.000
HE ATTACHES THE TUBE
WITH TIE WRAPS

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.434
SO IT DOESN'T GET TANGLED
INSIDE THE HULL.

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:17.367
HE INSTALLS A JAM CLEAT
FOR THE ROPE,

00:03:17.367 --> 00:03:20.067
THAT WILL ALLOW THE PADDLER
TO MANUALLY CONTROL

00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:21.501
THE ANCHOR FROM THE DECK.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:28.033
♪♪

00:03:28.033 --> 00:03:31.033
THE HULL'S CURED
VINYL ESTER RESIN

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:35.033
IS NOW FIRMLY BONDED TO THE
STRUCTURAL LAMINATE.

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:38.133
THE ASSEMBLER APPLIES THE
EXPANDING ADHESIVE,

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:41.634
AND POSITIONS AN EXPANDED
POLYPROPYLENE FOAM STRINGER

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:42.901
INSIDE THE HULL.

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:45.968
THE FOAM STRINGERS ARE THE
BACKBONE OF THE BOARD.

00:03:45.968 --> 00:03:49.234
THEY SUPPORT THE WEIGHT
OF THE PADDLER ON DECK,

00:03:49.234 --> 00:03:52.367
WHILE KEEPING THE BOARD
AS LIGHT AS POSSIBLE.

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:55.100
USING A NYLON WEDGE
AND RUBBER MALLET,

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:58.234
THE ASSEMBLER REMOVES THE MOLD
FROM THE HULL.

00:03:58.234 --> 00:04:00.968
SINCE THE HULL IS SO
LIGHTWEIGHT,

00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:04.667
TWO ASSEMBLERS CAN LIFT
AND FLIP IT ONTO AS CART.

00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:07.901
AN ASSEMBLER TRIMS OFF THE
EXCESS LAMINATE

00:04:07.901 --> 00:04:12.000
USING AN AIR CUTTER FITTED WITH
A DIAMOND CUTTING BLADE.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.901
HE LEVELS THE FOAM STRINGERS
WITH A FILE BLADE,

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:20.701
ENSURING THE TIGHTEST POSSIBLE
FIT BETWEEN THE HULL AND DECK.

00:04:20.701 --> 00:04:24.133
HE APPLIES EXPANDING FOAM
ADHESIVE ON THE STRINGERS

00:04:24.133 --> 00:04:26.801
BEFORE HE PLACES THE DECK
ON THE FOAM,

00:04:26.801 --> 00:04:28.701
WITH THE HELP OF A COWORKER.

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:32.901
THE ADHESIVE QUICKLY BINDS THE
PARTS TOGETHER.

00:04:32.901 --> 00:04:36.100
THE VINYL RUB RAIL,
DESIGNED AS A SIDE PROTECTION,

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:39.067
MASKS THE JOINT
BETWEEN THE DECK AND THE HULL.

00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:44.868
THE HULL CONTAINS
A DRY STORAGE HATCH

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:47.634
WHERE THE ONBOARD BATTERY
IS HOUSED.

00:04:47.634 --> 00:04:51.634
THE 8-AMP HOUR BATTERY CAN
ACTIVATE THE POWER POLE --

00:04:51.634 --> 00:04:54.968
A MICRO ANCHOR DESIGNED
FOR SHALLOW WATERS.

00:04:54.968 --> 00:04:58.834
IN DEEPER WATERS,
A PADDLER CAN MANUALLY ACTIVATE

00:04:58.834 --> 00:05:03.033
THE INTERNAL ANCHOR SYSTEM WITH
A 16-FOOT NYLON CORD.

00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:06.634
FINALLY, THIS BOARD IS READY
TO HIT THE WATER.

